   "name": "potato.md",
   "text": "title: Potato\naka: potatoes, pomme de terre, kartoffel, seed potato\ntags: plant vegetable food garden\nwarn: Green skin, sprouts, leaves and the small green berries are toxic. Cut away green parts and eyes, and discard very green potatoes.\nsee: sowing-calendar, seed-saving\nsource: compiled from general gardening references, verify before relying on it\n\nOne of the most productive staple crops for a small garden. Easy to grow and stores for months.\n\n## grow\n1. Two to four weeks before planting, set seed potatoes in a light, cool place so they grow short, sturdy sprouts.\n2. Plant from April to early May in Central Europe, when the soil is no longer frozen.\n3. Plant about 10 cm deep, 30 to 40 cm apart, in rows about 70 cm apart.\n4. When shoots reach about 20 cm, pile soil around them, leaving only the tops visible. Repeat once or twice. Tubers exposed to light turn green.\n5. Water in dry spells, especially while flowering.\n\n## harvest\nEarly potatoes: dig from when the plants flower. Main crop: when the leaves have turned yellow and died back, wait about two weeks so the skins harden, then dig on a dry day.\n\n## store\nDry them briefly in the shade, then store in the dark in a cool, frost-free place, ideally 4 to 8 °C. Light turns them green. Keep away from apples, which make them sprout.\n\n## cook\nAlways cook potatoes. Boil, bake or roast.\n\n## also said\n- green potato\n- potatoes\n- seed potatoes\n- can i eat potatoes that are green\n- the potatoes have long sprouts are they still ok\n- my potatoes turned green in the bag\n- how do I plant potatoes\n- how deep do potatoes go in the ground\n- spacing between potato rows\n- when to plant potatoes in germany\n- should I let seed potatoes sprout first\n- chitting potatoes\n- piling soil around potato plants why\n- earthing up potatoes\n- potato plants are 20 cm tall now what\n- do potatoes need water when flowering\n- when to dig up potatoes\n- leaves turned yellow and died on my potato plants\n- new potatoes when can i harvest\n- how to store potatoes for winter\n- potatoes sprouting in the cellar\n- best temperature to keep potatoes\n- can i keep potatoes next to apples\n- potatoes rotted in storage\n- my kid ate the little green berries on the potato plant\n- are potato leaves poisonous\n- can you eat raw potato\n- cut off green parts of potato and eat the rest?\n- staple crop for small garden\n- how far apart do i plant seed potatoes\n- frost got into my potato store, are they ruined\n- the skin is still soft when I dig them\n- tiny green tomato like fruit on potato plant\n- potato eyes poisonous?\n- how much light do stored potatoes need\n- old man here, potatoes all green under the skin, throw away?\n"
