   "name": "water-filter.md",
   "text": "title: Filtering and settling water\naka: filter water, water filter, sand filter, charcoal filter, clean muddy water, cloudy water\ntags: water treatment\nwarn: Improvised filters make water clearer but do not reliably remove germs. Always boil, use bleach or SODIS after filtering.\nsee: water-boil, water-bleach, water-sodis\nsource: CDC, Making water safe in an emergency (cdc.gov/water-emergency); compiled from general survival references, verify before relying on it\n\nFiltering removes mud, sediment and some taste. It is a first step that makes disinfection work better, not a replacement for it.\n\n## how\nSettling:\n1. Fill a container and leave it still for several hours.\n2. Carefully pour or scoop the clear water from the top, leaving the sediment.\n\nCloth filter:\nPour the water through several layers of clean, tightly woven cloth.\n\nLayered filter (a cut bottle, bucket or sock):\n1. Make a small hole at the bottom and cover it with cloth.\n2. Add layers from bottom to top: fine gravel, crushed charcoal from a wood fire (not ash, not briquettes), fine sand, then coarse sand or gravel on top.\n3. Pour water in slowly at the top and collect it below.\n4. Throw away the first water that comes through.\n5. Disinfect the result.\n\n```\n      dirty water in\n           |\n    |~~~~~~v~~~~~~|\n    |  coarse sand |  <- or gravel, catches big dirt\n    |..............|\n    |  fine sand   |\n    |..............|\n    |  charcoal    |  <- crushed, from a wood fire\n    |..............|\n    |  fine gravel |\n    |__cloth_______|\n           |\n           v\n     filtered water  -> still disinfect it\n```\n\n## safety\nMost portable filters do not remove viruses. Charcoal from a fire is not the same as activated carbon and removes much less. Chemicals and fuel pass through improvised filters.\n\n## also said\n- water filter\n- muddy water\n- sand filter\n- charcoal filter\n- the water is brown and full of dirt\n- how do i make a filter with a bottle\n- diy water filter with sand and charcoal\n- what layers in a homemade filter\n- order of sand gravel charcoal in filter\n- can I use ash from the fire in the filter\n- bbq briquettes for water filter?\n- charcoal from campfire same as activated carbon?\n- does a homemade filter make water safe to drink\n- is filtered water safe without boiling\n- muddy river water how to clean it\n- let the water sit to settle the mud\n- how long to let water settle\n- cloudy water what do i do first\n- filter water through a t-shirt\n- cloth to strain water\n- sock filter for water\n- first water through filter is dirty, throw away?\n- my portable filter does it remove viruses\n- camping filter kills viruses?\n- water full of sediment from the flood\n- remove dirt from pond water\n- bucket filter how to make\n- filter water to make it clearer before treating\n- the water looks like chocolate milk\n- make a filter from a cut plastic bottle\n- does a charcoal filter remove chemicals\n- sand filter still smells like petrol\n- filtering removes bad taste?\n- why is my homemade filter water still cloudy\n- clear the water so bleach works better\n- strain lake water through fabric\n"
